<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alfred I, Prince of Windisch-Grätz</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1787">1787</a>–<a href="/years/1862">1862</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Alfred Windisch-Grätz, Alfred Windischgrätz, Alfred, Prince of Windisch-Grätz</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alfred, Prince of Windisch-Grätz, was an Austrian field marshal who led the counter-revolution of 1848. He crushed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prague">Prague</a> uprising in June and retook <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a> from the revolutionaries in October 1848, then advanced into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a>, but after defeats by the Hungarian army he was relieved of command in April 1849.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alfred-i-prince-of-windisch-gratz.jpg" alt="Alfred I, Prince of Windisch-Grätz" width="320" height="526" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ludwig Angerer · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Windischgr%C3%A4tz,_Alfred_I._F%C3%BCrst_von.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
